# CoApply — local personal-data tokens for audit.sh §1   (EXAMPLE — copy, don't edit in place)
#
#   cp scripts/audit-pii-local.example scripts/.audit-pii-local
#
# `.audit-pii-local` is gitignored and never published. Put your own identifying
# tokens here so the audit can catch them if one ever leaks into the engine.
#
# Why this file is separate: audit.sh is public. A list of your employers and
# internal project names committed into a public script IS the leak it's meant to
# prevent - it publishes your work history and shows the engine was built around
# one person. Structural patterns that name nobody stay in audit.sh; the personal
# ones live here, on your machine only.
#
# Format: one extended-regex (ERE) per line. Blank lines and #comments ignored.
# Every line is OR'd together and run against the engine's scanned paths.
#
# Without this file the audit still runs - it reports §1 as structural-only rather
# than claiming a clean it didn't earn. Same rule as check-letter.sh: "I couldn't
# check" is never printed as "clean".
#
# Add the things that would identify YOU, for example:
#   - your home directory path
#   - each employer's name (\b...\b so short names don't match inside other words)
#   - internal product/feature names only your team would recognize
#   - a former employer's domain
#   - any account, tenant, or workspace ID you've pasted while testing

# /Users/yourname
# \bAcmeCorp\b
# \bNorthwind\b
# examplecompany\.com
# Widget Wizard
# [0-9a-f]{16,}
